[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-repair-decision :complete-repair-execution :declare-bicycle-roadworthy :clear-bicycle-for-sale :finalize-roadworthiness-clearance :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage" "2799007224-cloud-itonami-isco-7224-metal-polishers-wheel-grinders-tool-sharpeners-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the repair" "complete the repair" "finalize the repair" "finalize the repair job" "declare the bicycle roadworthy" "declare the bicycle safe to ride" "clear the bicycle for sale" "declare the bicycle roadworthy and cleared for sale" "certify the bicycle as roadworthy" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007234, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :repair-services/bicycle-workshop-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:repairer-verified :shop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7234", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007234: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7234 Bicycle and Related Repairers workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7234\n-- Bicycle and Related Repairers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of\nthe rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-8 already landed:\n48 occupations so far).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7234\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7234\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Bicycle and Related Repairers\" -- confirming\nthe premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity`\nwas `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed\nat `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7234` (`gh api` 404 confirmed\nbefore scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote\nthe `7234` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nBicycle and related repairers perform standard mechanical repair work\nwith standard workshop hazards (tools, moving parts) -- lower stakes\nthan motorized-vehicle or aviation mechanics, but still requiring a\nclean coordination/execution boundary. The controlling constraint for\nthis vertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any\nop that directly finalizes a repair-execution decision, or a\nroadworthiness-clearance decision (declaring a bicycle safe to ride or\nsell), or overrides a shop safety officer's judgment -- those\ndecisions must always be a hard permanent block, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to WORKSHOP\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs repair\nwork itself or makes roadworthiness-clearance decisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)\n(Metal Moulders and Coremakers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, a\nclosely-related workshop-mechanical safety pattern) -- cloned and read\nin full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7234` as an OSS bicycle-\nrepair-workshop scheduling/logistics-coordination actor for bicycle\nand related repairers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture\nas every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Bicycle\nRepair Coordination Advisor -| BikeCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct repair-execution or roadworthiness-\nclearance authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising a repair-execution\ndecision, a roadworthiness-clearance decision, or any override of a\nshop safety officer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- repair-job/inventory/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/bay scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a mechanical-hazard/equipment-\n  condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- bicycle-parts procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nrepair-execution decision, a roadworthiness-clearance decision, or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are **structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind\nescalation -- an op such as `:declare-bicycle-roadworthy` cannot even\nbe proposed by the reference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for`\nfunctions only ever emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any\ncode path (a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving\nfork) ever produced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD\ncheck (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A\nsecond, independent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names seven\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`bikecoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-repair-decision`, `:complete-repair-execution`,\n`:declare-bicycle-roadworthy`, `:clear-bicycle-for-sale`,\n`:finalize-roadworthiness-clearance`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`bikecoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-bicycle-roadworthy`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-clear-bicycle-for-sale`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-repair-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Repairer unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered repairer record (`:no-repairer`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the repairer is.\n2. **Shop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered repair shop/workshop (`:no-shop`). Together with check\n   1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   repairer/shop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the seven\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for a repair, a\n   roadworthiness-clearance decision, or overriding a shop safety\n   officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks repair-execution/roadworthiness-clearance/\n   safety-override language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a mechanical-hazard/\n  equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the concern\n  itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard data,\"\n  never \"here is what I recommend doing about workshop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  bicycle-parts order is not itself unsafe, unlike a repair-execution,\n  roadworthiness-clearance, or safety-officer-override attempt, which\n  is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs.\n  structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"bicycle\", \"repair\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a workshop coordination actor working\nadjacent to repair work necessarily discusses those concepts to do its\nscheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`bikecoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"finalize the repair\", \"declare\nthe bicycle roadworthy and cleared for sale\", \"override the shop\nsafety officer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`bikecoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for repairer ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nrepair-bay task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\")\nWITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`bikecoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7234\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7234` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7234`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 47 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-roadworthiness-clearance` that\n  is merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape some\n  earlier-wave actors use for lower-stakes approval ops): rejected\n  outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  roadworthiness-clearance decision exists in the code path and is\n  merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this consequential\n  (declaring a bicycle safe to ride or sell), the capability itself\n  must not exist. The only op related to workshop-safety escalation is\n  `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/shop-\n  safety-officer attention and never itself decides, authorizes, or\n  defers a repair-execution or roadworthiness-clearance decision for\n  later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the\n  transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check some financial-domain actors\n  use): rejected per the task's explicit domain design -- an\n  over-threshold bicycle-parts order is not itself unsafe, so it is\n  handled as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  repair-execution/roadworthiness-clearance/safety-officer-override\n  class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. [\"bicycle\" \"repair\"\n  \"safety\"]): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses bicycle/\n  repair/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so\n  a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Naming the excluded-op set after \"shop safety officer\" only, vs.\n  also naming a second distinct authority figure (mirroring some\n  physical-safety-domain actors' dual safety-officer/foreman split):\n  rejected -- the task's domain design names only \"a shop safety\n  officer's judgment\" as the authority figure for this vertical, so a\n  single `:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment` op (plus a generic\n  `:override-safety-officer-judgment` alias and matching phrase\n  variants) fully covers the specified scope without inventing an\n  unspecified second authority role.\n- Merging `repairer` and `shop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered repairer AND independently-registered\n  shop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a repairer/shop record\n  must be independently verified/registered before any action and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- repair-job/inventory/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered repairer AND\n   shop (`:no-repairer`/`:no-shop`). Not a repair-execution or\n   roadworthiness-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/bay scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a repair-execution or roadworthiness-clearance\n   decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such\n   attempt via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action`\n   content check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any\n   conclusion about a specific repair or a bicycle's roadworthiness --\n   it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a mechanical-hazard/\n   equipment-condition concern to a human/shop safety officer; ALWAYS\n   escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- bicycle-parts procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a repair-execution or\n   roadworthiness-clearance decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na repair-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with or completing a\nspecific repair job), a roadworthiness-clearance decision (e.g.\ndeclaring a bicycle roadworthy or cleared for sale), or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`bikecoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) seven\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`bikecoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`bikecoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-bicycle-roadworthy`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-clear-bicycle-for-sale`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-repair-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`bikecoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to finalize a repair, declare a bicycle roadworthy and\ncleared for sale, or override a shop safety officer's judgment even\nvia an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`bikecoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-declare-roadworthy-and-cleared-for-sale`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 47, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Bicycle Repair Workshop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :repairer-verification :shop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7234", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7234", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7234], :test/simulator :bikecoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7234 \u2014 Bicycle and Related Repairers Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7234}]
